WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.933
Salary reality check, India, 2026.

2
00:00:04.233 --> 00:00:09.800
Here is what AI roles actually pay, and why a capable engineer has unusual leverage.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.867
Here is the ladder, from the bottom.

4
00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:17.433
A junior engineer with up to two years earns eight to fifteen lakh per year.

5
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:21.500
Mid-level, two to four years, is fifteen to thirty five lakh.

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.167
Senior, four to six years, is thirty five to sixty lakh.

7
00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:30.500
An architect or staff engineer with six plus years earns fifty to eighty plus lakh.

8
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.800
And a principal scientist, eight plus years, reaches eighty lakh to one crore and more.

9
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
But title is not the biggest lever.

10
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.500
Company type matters more than title.

11
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.933
Look at the two sides.

12
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:49.267
Product companies pay roughly two to three times what service firms pay for the same work.

13
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:56.567
GCCs, like Google, Microsoft, Amazon and Goldman in Bangalore and Hyderabad, are the top payers.

14
00:00:56.867 --> 00:01:01.533
And funded AI startups compete at twenty five to forty lakh for strong talent.

15
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:04.033
Now the demand side.

16
00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:09.306
Reportedly there is roughly one qualified candidate for every two AI roles.

17
00:01:09.306 --> 00:01:10.433
That is leverage.

18
00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:12.767
So where do you stand?

19
00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:16.867
Your band is the mid-level row, fifteen to thirty five lakh.

20
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.567
The top of that row overlaps with senior pay.

21
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:26.667
Getting to twenty five to thirty five lakh is about evidence, not years: shipped systems with measured impact.

22
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:28.572
Let's recap.

23
00:01:28.572 --> 00:01:31.333
Pay climbs from eight lakh to a crore and more.

24
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:33.167
Company type beats title.

25
00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:36.700
There is one qualified candidate for every two roles.

26
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.533
And evidence, not years, moves you up.

27
00:01:39.533 --> 00:01:42.067
Next up: the six month execution plan.
